#: ../../source/docs/systemid-model-development.rst:270
#: dbe2115faf644b5faf712c5290b05768
msgid ""
"The system of a quadcopter is inherently unstable. Slight modeling errors"
" or unconsidered external inputs of the real system lead to divergence of"
" the axis models [#f7]_. Since a model does never fully reproduce the "
"behavior of the real system, the model validation is conducted in closed-"
"loop with the same stabilize controller used during the test flights. For"
" the validation test runs, the closed-loop model is given the same input "
"signals that were given to the real system, which are the references for "
"the stabilize controller (desired angle or rate in case of the yaw axis)."
" The outputs of the models, namely the angular rates, are then compared "
"to the measured system outputs during real flight. First, it is examined "
"if the models reproduce the test signals, i.e. the frequency-sweeps. The "
"desired angles of the stabilize controller are set to zero and the sweeps"
" are directly added to the output of the rate controllers."
msgstr ""

